To determine how many vans Nancy's class will need for their field trip to the zoo, we start by calculating the total number of people going. There are 12 students and 3 adults, which gives:

$$
12 \text{ students} + 3 \text{ adults} = 15 \text{ people}
$$

Next, we divide the total number of people by the capacity of each van. Each van can hold 5 people:

$$
\frac{15 \text{ people}}{5 \text{ people per van}} = 3 \text{ vans}
$$

Since 15 is exactly divisible by 5, there is no need to round up. Therefore, the class will need exactly 3 vans to transport all the people.

$$
\boxed{3}
$$

